model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "The acceptance-pool route is reached only with an envelope of its own kind signed with the current pool signing key, under production-ops' bounds: the browser host as target, at most 5 s early, at most 60 s to live, an id of at most 128 characters and a body of at most 64 KiB. No session, cookie, API key or MCP identity participates, and every answer is a fixed body with a closed refusal word. A dry run seals a plan with production-ops' artifact protection; an apply needs that plan's checksum, the exact GO for it, the same target, release and database, a plan at most an hour old and, on a first apply, unchanged preconditions. Progress lives in the existing production-ops receipts table under the acceptance organization, with no schema change: the receipt names every envelope that acted on it, refuses a repeated one without writing, and holds a lease that a live holder never loses and that another apply takes over only after it runs out, resuming after the last recorded step. Every write to the receipt is fenced by the lease. A setup never resumes once a teardown has claimed it, and a teardown waits out a running setup. The emulated upstream's host comes only from the deploy's value; a setup refuses when it is unset, when the workflow's digest of its own origin differs from the digest of the host the server builds, or when the upstream key does not have the upstream's own shape. The key reaches only the account's encrypted token, never a receipt, plan or answer. The pool belongs to one kept identity, user and organization acceptance with an undeliverable address, written only by this route and only where absent, in one serializable transaction that deletes every lifecycle job and welcome email its inserts queued before it commits. It refuses rows with other bytes, a used slug or address, any sign-in or credential row, any other member or membership, a removal or a waiting job. Better Auth refuses any session or account for it, the daily seat reconcile never names it and seat sync returns before any billing call, release rollouts queue it no member job, and the route forces the analytics sink off."
    }
  }
}
